      "problem": "Find $p$ if $-2$ is a root of $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+6x-2p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=-2$ is a root, we have $f(-2)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=-2,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)^{2}+6(-2)-2p & =0 \\\\ 20-12-2p & =0 \\\\ 8-2p & =0 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
